Package: chadtab
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8)
Suggests: emacs-nox | emacs
Maintainer: Corwin Brust <corwin@bru.st>
Homepage: https://chadtab.com
Description: successor to cron, with its own record and a view
 chadtab runs scheduled work from one readable table on GNU/Linux and on
 Windows alike, keeps a JSON record of every run, catches up on runs missed
 while the machine was down, and shows how its jobs have been going (chadtab
 top; M-x chadtab-status in Emacs). Beside C4 it writes what a job learned
 into a registry with two writers that check each other.
